  "notes": "SYNTHETIC fixture. Borrower B is the WATCH / deteriorating-trend case (control contrast to the breach cases). Total Net Leverage = total_net_debt / consolidated_ebitda. EBITDA is flat at 50.0 across all three quarters (recomputed from operating_profit 25.0 + D&A 22.0 + exceptional 3.0 = 50.0, every add-back allowed, so certified == recomputed and there is NO drift/conflict). Consolidated Total Net Debt climbs 200.0 -> 210.0 -> 220.0, driven by rising RCF drawings (40 -> 50 -> 60) with term loan flat at 180 and cash flat at 20 (net debt = 180 + revolver - 20). Leverage therefore creeps 4.00x -> 4.20x -> 4.40x against a flat 5.00x ceiling and NEVER breaches (headroom 1.00 / 0.80 / 0.60x). WATCH is trend-based: watch_rule.deteriorating_periods=3 fires at b-p3 on the third consecutive rise, NOT on proximity (0.60x headroom > 0.25x trigger). field_map_fingerprint is identical across all three periods, documenting zero schema drift. expected_assessment is a test oracle only and is not read by assess(). Arithmetic per period: P1 200.0/50.0=4.00; P2 210.0/50.0=4.20; P3 220.0/50.0=4.40."
